3.17 Chapter Summary
This chapter has described the implementation of the Climate-Smart Improved Kienyeji Chicken Broiler Production Enterprise from project establishment to routine management. The project demonstrated that proper planning, good housing, adequate nutrition, effective disease control, accurate record keeping, and climate-smart management practices contribute significantly to successful poultry production. Despite experiencing a mortality of nine birds, the project achieved an 85% survival rate, producing 51 healthy birds for marketing. The next chapter presents the marketing strategy, value addition, financial analysis, profitability, sustainability, and recommendations.

